+| `COMPLIR_URL` | Server-side | Optional. CompliR host for recipient screening before a payment is sent; unset disables it. See below. |
+
+## Optional: CompliR counterparty screening
+
+Set `COMPLIR_URL` to a [CompliR](https://github.com/mrnetwork0001/complir) host and the Pay button calls the `screenRecipientAction` server action before the user operation is signed. It reads the recipient's risk tier from `GET /api/v1/attestation/<address>` (free; tiers are mirrored to the CompliR registry on [Arc mainnet](https://explorer.arc.network/address/0xA82EDb5e111c31C63E06EF0007f2fa1a9e7EB30d)). `HIGH` stops the payment with a "Transaction failed" toast; `LOW`/`MEDIUM` send as before. A CompliR timeout or outage fails open with a server warning. Because the user operation is signed in the browser, this is a UX guard, not an enforcement boundary. The paid `POST /api/v1/screen` (x402, 0.01 USDC on Arc) returns a fresh verdict with reasons and recommended limits and is the upgrade path.
 
 ## User Accounts
 
